      bullet([bold("1.  "), normal("Receive and own WindowEnvelope instances transferred from WindowDispatcher")], "numbers"),
      bullet([bold("2.  "), normal("Assign each envelope a unique instance ID and maintain the registry of all live envelopes")], "numbers"),
      bullet([bold("3.  "), normal("Own and delegate to WindowHierarchy for all window relationship tracking")], "numbers"),
      bullet([bold("4.  "), normal("Detect significant window lifecycle events \u2014 particularly last-window-closed \u2014 and surface them to GUIEngine")], "numbers"),
      spacer(80),
      para([italic("Nothing else. If a responsibility does not clearly fit into one of those buckets, it does not belong here.")]),
      spacer(160),
      rule(),

      // What it owns
      h1("What WindowCoordinator Owns"),

      h2("The Live Envelope Registry"),
      para([
        normal("The coordinator maintains the authoritative registry of all live "),
        mono("WindowEnvelope"),
        normal(" instances, keyed by their unique instance ID. This registry is the runtime answer to \u201Cwhat windows currently exist.\u201D")
      ]),
      spacer(80),
      para([
        normal("Each envelope in the registry carries two IDs: its own unique "),
        bold("instance ID"),
        normal(", assigned by the coordinator at the moment of receipt, and the "),
        bold("factory ID"),
        normal(" of the "),
        mono("WindowFactory"),
        normal(" that produced it, embedded at dispatch time. The instance ID identifies the specific live window. The factory ID identifies the kind of window it is. Both are stable for the lifetime of the envelope.")
      ]),
      spacer(80),
      para([
        normal("The registry supports two natural query patterns that fall directly out of this dual-ID structure:")
      ]),
      bullet([
        bold("Lookup by instance ID: "),
        normal("Retrieve a specific live envelope directly. Used for targeted operations such as resolving a parent handle during subsidiary window construction.")
      ]),
      bullet([
        bold("Filter by factory ID: "),
        normal("Retrieve all live envelopes that were produced by a given factory. Used for single-instance enforcement and for any application logic that wants to reason about all open windows of a particular kind.")
      ]),
      spacer(120),

      h2("WindowHierarchy"),
      para([
        normal("The coordinator owns a "),
        mono("WindowHierarchy"),
        normal(" instance that maintains the parent-child relationship graph across all live envelopes. This is a dedicated type rather than data scattered across individual envelopes, keeping relationship logic centralized and the coordinator\u2019s own code readable.")
      ]),
      spacer(80),
      para([
        normal("Relationships are tracked by instance ID. A parent envelope maps to a collection of child instance IDs, supporting the one-to-many cardinality that GUI window hierarchies naturally exhibit. Individual envelopes carry no relationship data themselves \u2014 the graph lives entirely inside "),
        mono("WindowHierarchy"),
        normal(".")
      ]),
      spacer(80),
      para([
        normal("Chevron does not attempt to manage window lifetime cascades directly. GUI frameworks handle the destruction of subsidiary windows when their parent closes, provided the windows were composed correctly at construction time. "),
        mono("WindowHierarchy"),
        normal("\u2019s role is to keep Chevron\u2019s own bookkeeping consistent after the framework has acted \u2014 not to duplicate or compete with what the framework already does well.")
      ]),
      spacer(160),
      rule(),

      // Identity assignment
      h1("Instance Identity Assignment"),
      para([
        normal("When the coordinator receives a new "),
        mono("WindowEnvelope"),
        normal(" from the dispatcher, its first act is to assign that envelope a unique sequential instance ID. This ID is the envelope\u2019s stable identity within Chevron for its entire lifetime.")
      ]),
      spacer(80),
      para([
        normal("Instance IDs and factory IDs serve different purposes and must not be confused. A factory ID identifies a registration \u2014 it is fixed at "),
        mono("WindowFactory"),
        normal(" submission time and shared by every envelope that factory ever produces. An instance ID identifies a specific live window \u2014 it is assigned at receipt time and unique across all envelopes regardless of which factory produced them.")
      ]),
      spacer(80),
      para([
        normal("This distinction is what makes the single-instance query clean: the dispatcher asks the coordinator whether any live envelope carries a given "),
        italic("factory"),
        normal(" ID. The coordinator answers by scanning its registry. No instance ID is involved in that query \u2014 only the factory ID embedded in each envelope at dispatch time.")
      ]),
      spacer(160),
      rule(),

      // Relationship to WindowDispatcher
      h1("Relationship to WindowDispatcher"),
      para([
        normal("The coordinator is aware of the dispatcher but the dispatcher is not aware of the coordinator. This one-way dependency is intentional.")
      ]),
      spacer(80),
      para([
        normal("The dispatcher\u2019s only need to reach the coordinator is to verify single-instance constraints before firing a factory. This is achieved through a narrow query interface \u2014 likely dependency-injected by "),
        mono("GUIEngine"),
        normal(" at construction time \u2014 that exposes nothing beyond a simple membership check: \u201Cdoes any live envelope carry this factory ID?\u201D The dispatcher calls this query and receives a yes or no. It has no further visibility into the coordinator\u2019s state.")
      ]),
      spacer(80),
      para([
        normal("The coordinator, by contrast, is a full participant in the window lifecycle. It receives envelopes, maintains the registry, owns the hierarchy, and surfaces lifecycle events. Its awareness of the dispatcher is structural \u2014 it understands that envelopes arrive from a dispatcher \u2014 but it does not hold a reference to the dispatcher or call into it.")
      ]),
      spacer(160),
      rule(),

      // Relationship to GUIEngine
      h1("Relationship to GUIEngine"),
      para([
        normal("The coordinator operates entirely within "),
        mono("GUIEngine\u2019s"),
        normal(" internal boundary. User code does not interact with it directly. All operations that require coordinator involvement \u2014 querying live windows, establishing parent-child relationships, responding to window closure events \u2014 pass through the engine\u2019s own API.")
      ]),
      spacer(80),
      para([
        normal("This is particularly relevant for subsidiary window construction. When user code requests a subsidiary window through "),
        mono("GUIEngine"),
        normal(", the engine resolves the parent envelope via the coordinator, assembles the "),
        mono("WindowInitContext"),
        normal(" with the parent\u2019s underlying window handle, and instructs the dispatcher to fire. The coordinator then receives the new envelope, registers it, and records the parent-child relationship in "),
        mono("WindowHierarchy"),
        normal(". The coordinator never reaches out to perform this orchestration itself \u2014 that belongs to the engine.")
      ]),
      spacer(160),
      rule(),

      // Lifecycle events
      h1("Lifecycle Event Awareness"),
      para([
        normal("The coordinator is the component best positioned to detect meaningful window lifecycle events because it has visibility over the full population of live envelopes at all times.")
      ]),
      spacer(80),
      para([
        normal("The most significant event is last-window-closed. When the final envelope leaves the registry \u2014 whether because the main window closed and the framework initiated shutdown, or because the application explicitly destroyed all windows \u2014 the coordinator surfaces this to "),
        mono("GUIEngine"),
        normal(", which may in turn signal "),
        mono("AppProcess"),
        normal(" to begin the shutdown sequence.")
      ]),
      spacer(80),
      para([
        normal("The coordinator does not initiate shutdown itself. It observes, records, and notifies. The decision of what to do in response to a lifecycle event belongs to "),
        mono("GUIEngine"),
        normal(" and ultimately to "),
        mono("AppProcess"),
        normal(".")
      ]),
      spacer(160),
      rule(),

      // Shutdown and teardown
      h1("Shutdown and Teardown"),
      para([italic("Teardown is not the inverse of construction.")]),
      spacer(80),
      para([
        normal("When "),
        mono("GUIEngine"),
        normal(" begins its shutdown sequence, the coordinator winds down all live envelopes in a controlled order. Subsidiary windows are addressed before their parents to avoid acting against what the framework has already handled. "),
        mono("WindowHierarchy"),
        normal(" provides the traversal order.")
      ]),
      spacer(80),
      para([
        normal("Once an envelope has been wound down, it is removed from the registry and its entry in "),
        mono("WindowHierarchy"),
        normal(" is cleared. The coordinator\u2019s state is fully drained before "),
        mono("GUIEngine"),
        normal(" proceeds with framework deinitialization.")
      ]),
      spacer(80),
      para([
        normal("At the end of teardown, no envelopes remain. The coordinator is empty but still valid \u2014 it does not destroy itself. Its lifetime is governed by the "),
        mono("GUIEngine"),
        normal(" that owns it.")
      ]),
      spacer(160),
      rule(),

      // Error handling
      h1("Error Handling Philosophy"),
      para("WindowCoordinator should:"),
      bullet("Fail fast on any operation that assumes a live envelope that does not exist in the registry"),
      bullet("Never silently drop an envelope or allow one to leak outside the registry"),
      bullet("Refuse any post-shutdown registration or query that implies new window activity"),
      bullet("Surface lifecycle events reliably \u2014 a missed last-window-closed notification is a correctness failure"),
      spacer(80),
      para([
        bold("Note: "),
        normal("The boundary between returned error codes and thrown exceptions follows the same open question as the rest of the library \u2014 deferred pending library-wide error handling strategy decisions.")
      ]),
      spacer(160),
      rule(),

      // Open questions
      h1("Open Questions and Deferred Decisions"),
      para("The following are known open questions that are intentionally deferred:"),
      spacer(80),
      bullet([
        bold("WindowDispatcher / WindowCoordinator handoff mechanism: "),
        normal("The precise protocol by which a newly constructed WindowEnvelope transfers ownership from the dispatcher to the coordinator \u2014 including the exact call sequence and any synchronization requirements \u2014 has not been designed.")
      ]),
      bullet([
        bold("Single-instance query interface: "),
        normal("The narrow interface through which WindowDispatcher queries the coordinator for factory ID membership has not been formally defined. The shape is clear \u2014 a boolean membership check by factory ID \u2014 but the precise C++ surface is deferred.")
      ]),
      bullet([
        bold("WindowHierarchy design: "),
        normal("The internal structure of WindowHierarchy \u2014 how the parent-to-children mapping is stored, how traversal order is determined at teardown, and what query API it exposes to the coordinator \u2014 is deferred to dedicated design work on that type.")
      ]),
      bullet([
        bold("Lifecycle event notification mechanism: "),
        normal("How the coordinator surfaces events such as last-window-closed to GUIEngine has not been defined. Candidates include callbacks, an observer interface, or a direct method call on GUIEngine. This is deferred pending broader decisions on Chevron\u2019s internal event and notification patterns.")
      ]),
      bullet([
        bold("Framework cascade verification: "),
        normal("The mechanism by which Chevron verifies that the underlying framework has correctly handled subsidiary window teardown before cleaning up coordinator records has not been designed.")
      ]),
      bullet([
        bold("Error handling boundary: "),
        normal("Follows the same open question as AppProcess, GUIEngine, WindowDispatcher, and WindowFactory. Deferred pending library-wide decisions.")
      ]),
      spacer(160),
      rule(),

      // Footer
      new Paragraph({
        children: [new TextRun({ text: "Chevron Library \u2014 Internal Design Documentation", font: FONT, size: 18, color: "AAAAAA", italics: true })],
        alignment: AlignmentType.CENTER,
        spacing: { before: 160 }
      })
    ]
  }]
});

Packer.toBuffer(doc).then(buffer => {
  fs.writeFileSync('/mnt/user-data/outputs/WindowCoordinator_Class_Description.docx', buffer);
  console.log('Done');
});
