        normal(" concern \u2014 but it is the authority that decides when the boundary opens and when it closes.")
      ]),
      spacer(160),
      rule(),

      // What problem it solves
      h1("What Problem AppProcess Is Solving"),
      para("Without AppProcess, users would have to:"),
      bullet([normal("Manually sequence GUI backend startup")]),
      bullet([normal("Manually handle error paths")]),
      bullet([normal("Manually ensure shutdown correctness")]),
      bullet([normal("Manually guarantee invariants such as "), italic("\u201Cyou cannot start twice\u201D"), normal(" and "), italic("\u201Cyou cannot shutdown before start\u201D")]),
      spacer(80),
      para("Chevron\u2019s core promise is:"),
      blockquote("\u201CIf the application is running, it is running correctly.\u201D"),
      para([mono("AppProcess"), normal(" is the class that enforces that promise.")]),
      spacer(160),
      rule(),

      // Core responsibilities
      h1("Core Responsibilities (Non-Negotiable)"),
      para("AppProcess has exactly three responsibilities:"),
      spacer(80),
      bullet([bold("1.  "), normal("Own the application lifecycle")], "numbers"),
      bullet([bold("2.  "), normal("Own exactly one active GUI engine")], "numbers"),
      bullet([bold("3.  "), normal("Enforce valid sequencing")], "numbers"),
      spacer(80),
      para([italic("Nothing else. If a responsibility does not clearly fit into one of those buckets, it does not belong here.")]),
      spacer(160),
      rule(),

      // Lifetime
      h1("Lifetime of AppProcess"),
      bullet("Constructed near the entry point (user discretion)"),
      bullet("Lives for the entire process"),
      bullet("Destroyed at process exit"),
      spacer(80),
      para([
        normal("There should be "),
        bold("one instance per process"),
        normal(". The mechanism for enforcing this constraint is an open question \u2014 candidates include deleted copy/move constructors with documentation, or a runtime assertion on construction. This is deferred pending broader decisions on library-wide enforcement patterns.")
      ]),
      spacer(160),
      rule(),

      // Interaction with GUIEngine
      h1("How AppProcess Interacts With a GUI Engine"),
      para([
        mono("AppProcess"),
        normal(" holds and drives exactly one "),
        bold("GUIEngine"),
        normal(" instance \u2014 the polymorphic interface contract between "),
        mono("AppProcess"),
        normal(" and all concrete GUI backend implementations. "),
        mono("AppProcess"),
        normal(" interacts with the engine exclusively through this interface and has no knowledge of the underlying framework.")
      ]),
