      bullet("Any framework-specific initialization or teardown logic"),
      spacer(160),
      rule(),

      // What GUIEngine does NOT own
      h1("What GUIEngine Deliberately Does Not Own"),
      para([italic("This is just as important as what it does own.")]),
      spacer(80),
      para("GUIEngine does not own:"),
      bullet("Application lifetime or process startup and exit"),
      bullet("Command line parsing beyond what the backend minimally requires"),
      bullet("Business logic of any kind"),
      bullet("Non-GUI services or infrastructure"),
      spacer(80),
      para([
        normal("That boundary keeps the layering clean. "),
        mono("AppProcess"),
        normal(" governs the process. "),
        mono("GUIEngine"),
        normal(" governs the GUI environment within it. Neither reaches into the other\u2019s domain.")
      ]),
      spacer(160),
      rule(),

      // Lifetime
      h1("Lifetime of GUIEngine"),
      para([
        mono("GUIEngine"),
        normal(" is constructed by the user as a concrete implementation, configured, and then committed to "),
        mono("AppProcess"),
        normal(". From that point forward, "),
        mono("AppProcess"),
        normal(" drives it exclusively through the "),
        mono("GUIEngine"),
        normal(" interface.")
      ]),
      spacer(120),

      h2("1. Construction"),
      para([
        normal("The user constructs a concrete engine (e.g. "),
        mono("chevron::wx::Engine"),
        normal("). At this point, no GUI framework calls have occurred and no global GUI state has been touched. Configuration is still mutable. This phase exists solely to prepare the engine for commitment.")
      ]),
      spacer(80),
      para([italic("Nothing GUI-visible exists yet.")]),
      spacer(120),

      h2("2. Commitment to AppProcess"),
      para([
        normal("Ownership transfers to "),
        mono("AppProcess"),
        normal(". Configuration is effectively locked. The engine is now the chosen backend for the lifetime of the process. Still no GUI initialization, no windows, no mainloop.")
      ]),
      spacer(120),

      h2("3. Initialization"),
      para([
        mono("AppProcess"),
        normal(" instructs the engine to initialize. This is where the GUI framework comes alive: the framework\u2019s application object is created, environment assumptions are validated, and internal subsystems are prepared. The mainloop has "),
        bold("not"),
        normal(" started. Windows do "),
        bold("not"),
        normal(" exist yet.")
      ]),
      spacer(80),
      para("If initialization fails:"),
      bullet("No mainloop starts"),
      bullet("No windows are created"),
      bullet("The application can still exit cleanly"),
      spacer(120),

      h2("4. Runtime Start"),
      para([bold("This is the point of no return.")]),
      spacer(80),
      para([
        mono("AppProcess"),
        normal(" calls "),
        mono("startRuntime()"),
        normal(". The engine materializes windows through "),
        mono("WindowDispatcher"),
        normal(", "),
        mono("WindowCoordinator"),
        normal(" begins tracking them, and the mainloop enters. From this moment, "),
        mono("startRuntime()"),
        normal(" blocks. Control flow is inside the GUI framework until shutdown.")
      ]),
      spacer(120),

      h2("5. Shutdown and Teardown"),
      para([italic("Shutdown is not the inverse of startup.")]),
      spacer(80),
      para([
        normal("Shutdown may be initiated by user code, by the GUI framework itself (e.g. the last window closes), or by "),
        mono("AppProcess"),
        normal(". The engine must support all three origins without the caller needing to coordinate them.")
      ]),
      spacer(80),
      para("During shutdown:"),
      bullet("The mainloop is stopped"),
      bullet([mono("WindowingSubsystem"), normal(" is destroyed before its referenced components")]),
      bullet([mono("WindowCoordinator"), normal(" winds down live windows in a controlled order")]),
      bullet("Per-window infrastructure is torn down with each window envelope"),
      bullet("The GUI framework is deinitialized"),
      bullet([normal("Control returns to "), mono("AppProcess")]),
      spacer(80),
      para([bold("Calling shutdown twice must be safe.")]),
      spacer(160),
      rule(),

      // Abstract base vs concrete — UPDATED
      h1("Abstract Base vs. Concrete Implementations"),
      para([
        normal("The base "),
        mono("GUIEngine"),
        normal(" class defines the lifecycle contract, ownership boundaries, and sequencing rules. It is the surface that "),
        mono("AppProcess"),
        normal(" sees and the only surface it is permitted to use.")
      ]),
      spacer(80),
      para([
        normal("Concrete implementations inherit from this base and are responsible for exactly one thing that varies per backend: how the framework is initialized, how its mainloop is controlled, and how it is torn down. Everything else \u2014 window dispatching, window coordination, the envelope model, the windowing subsystem projection \u2014 is handled at the base level and is not reimplemented per backend.")
      ]),
      spacer(80),
      para([
        normal("Concrete engines interact with the base infrastructure exclusively through "),
        bold("protected virtual lifecycle hooks"),
        normal(" \u2014 defined entry points such as post-initialization and post-runtime-start callbacks \u2014 rather than through direct access to "),
        mono("WindowDispatcher"),
        normal(", "),
        mono("WindowCoordinator"),
        normal(", or "),
        mono("WindowingSubsystem"),
        normal(". This keeps the internal components genuinely internal and ensures that concrete backends cannot interfere with Chevron\u2019s own orchestration of those components.")
      ]),
      spacer(80),
      para([
        normal("Adding a new backend is therefore a focused task: implement the framework-specific lifecycle and respond to the defined hooks where needed. The base class handles everything else.")
      ]),
      spacer(160),
      rule(),

      // Error handling
      h1("Error Handling Philosophy"),
      para("GUIEngine should:"),
      bullet("Fail fast on lifecycle misuse"),
      bullet("Return explicit status codes where applicable"),
      bullet("Never leave the GUI environment half-initialized or half-alive"),
      bullet("Throw on exceptional code paths"),
      spacer(80),
      para([
        bold("Note: "),
        normal("The precise boundary between returned error codes and thrown exceptions follows the same open question as AppProcess \u2014 deferred pending library-wide error handling strategy decisions.")
      ]),
      spacer(80),
      para("Examples of misuse that must be caught:"),
      bullet("Any GUI-bound operation attempted before initialization"),
      bullet("Starting the mainloop without a committed and initialized engine"),
      bullet("Initializing twice"),
      bullet("Window operations attempted after shutdown has begun"),
      spacer(160),
      rule(),

      // Public API shape — UPDATED
      h1("Public API Shape (Conceptual, Not Code)"),
      para([
        normal("From "),
        mono("AppProcess\u2019s"),
        normal(" perspective, the surface of "),
        mono("GUIEngine"),
        normal(" is intentionally narrow:")
      ]),
      spacer(80),
      bullet("Initialize the GUI framework"),
      bullet("Start the mainloop and block"),
      bullet("Accept a shutdown signal and tear down cleanly"),
      spacer(80),
      para([
        normal("All windowing operations \u2014 factory registration, window dispatch, live window queries, component access \u2014 are not part of "),
        mono("GUIEngine\u2019s"),
        normal(" direct API. They are surfaced through "),
        mono("WindowingSubsystem"),
        normal(" via the "),
        mono("windowing()"),
        normal(" accessor, which is the intended entry point for all user-facing windowing work. "),
        mono("AppProcess"),
        normal(" never touches this surface.")
      ]),
      spacer(160),
      rule(),

      // Open questions — UPDATED
      h1("Open Questions and Deferred Decisions"),
      para("The following are known open questions that are intentionally deferred:"),
      spacer(80),
      bullet([
        bold("WindowDispatcher / WindowCoordinator handoff mechanism: "),
        normal("The precise protocol by which a newly constructed WindowEnvelope transfers ownership from the dispatcher to the coordinator has not been designed.")
      ]),
      bullet([
        bold("Shutdown signal routing: "),
        normal("The precise mechanism by which a framework-initiated shutdown (e.g. last window closed) is communicated back to AppProcess has not been defined.")
      ]),
      bullet([
        bold("Protected hook surface shape: "),
        normal("The precise set of protected virtual lifecycle hooks that concrete engine implementations may override \u2014 their names, signatures, and sequencing guarantees \u2014 is a development-time detail deferred to implementation.")
      ]),
      bullet([
        bold("Future subsystem projections: "),
        normal("WindowingSubsystem is the first instance of the subsystem projection pattern on GUIEngine. Additional subsystems \u2014 event routing, view management, and others \u2014 will be added as the library grows. Their design is deferred to the appropriate phase of development.")
      ]),
      bullet([
        bold("Error handling boundary: "),
        normal("Follows the same open question as AppProcess. Deferred pending library-wide decisions.")
      ]),
      spacer(160),
      rule(),

      // Footer
      new Paragraph({
        children: [new TextRun({ text: "Chevron Library \u2014 Internal Design Documentation", font: FONT, size: 18, color: "AAAAAA", italics: true })],
        alignment: AlignmentType.CENTER,
        spacing: { before: 160 }
      })
    ]
  }]
});

Packer.toBuffer(doc).then(buffer => {
  fs.writeFileSync('/mnt/user-data/outputs/GUIEngine_Class_Description.docx', buffer);
  console.log('Done');
});
